WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.370
A parent asked me: does sleep

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.610
help my daughter's marks?

3
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.540
I had sleep hours and test

4
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.620
marks for our class.

5
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.020
Two numbers for each pupil.

6
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.430
How could I see if they go together?

7
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.310
Today: scatter plots, correlation, and why

8
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.850
together is not the same as cause.

9
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.750
A scatter plot puts one

10
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.150
measurement across and the other up.

11
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.880
Each pupil becomes one dot.

12
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.090
Sleep goes along the bottom, and

13
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.470
the mark goes up the side.

14
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.760
If the dots rise from left to right,

15
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.540
that is a positive relationship.

16
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.840
If they fall, it is negative, like

17
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.000
screen time late at night and marks.

18
00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.390
If they make a shapeless cloud,

19
00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.170
there is no relationship.

20
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.600
The correlation, called r, measures how

21
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.740
close the dots are to a straight line.

22
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.880
It goes from minus one to one.

23
00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:00.110
Near one is a strong positive pattern,

24
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.830
near zero is no straight-line pattern.

25
00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.870
Here is a famous pattern.

26
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.140
Ice cream sales and

27
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.980
drownings rise together.

28
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.760
Does ice cream make people drown?

29
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.130
No.

30
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.020
Hot weather brings both.

31
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.270
So when sleep and marks go together,

32
00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:23.590
ask what else could explain it.

33
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.640
Families with calm homes may give

34
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.240
children both more sleep and more

35
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.080
help with homework.

36
00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:31.870
Quick check!

37
00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.850
The dots lie very close to a

38
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.070
rising straight line.

39
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:37.850
Which r fits best?

40
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.580
About zero point nine.

41
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.770
Rising means positive, and close

42
00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.330
to a line means strong.

43
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.400
Minus zero point nine would be a

44
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.220
strong falling pattern.

45
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.560
In the app, open Scatter,

46
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.620
correlation and best fit.

47
00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.780
Tap to add pupils who study a lot but

48
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.320
score low, and watch r fall.

49
00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:03.130
Your turn.

50
00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.420
Pupils with more books at home get higher

51
00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.380
marks, with r of zero point six.

52
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.690
Does that prove books cause higher marks?

53
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.540
No, not on its own.

54
00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.530
Remember: a scatter plot shows two

55
00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.490
measurements, r measures how close they

56
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.810
are to a line, and correlation is not

57
00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.310
cause.

58
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.840
Always ask what else could explain it.

59
00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.010
Try it yourself: measure the

60
00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.950
height and arm span of five

61
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.790
people at home, and plot them.

62
00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.560
Is there a pattern, and does one

63
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.980
really cause the other?
